{%- comment -%}
  PERSONALIZATION FLOWS
  =====================

  Two kinds of visitor reach the product page, and they should not see the
  same page:

    quiz    — arrived via the landing page and completed the customization
              quiz, so they already know their formula and have already seen
              some of the story.
    direct  — landed on the product page cold. Generic wording, full story.

  Shopify caches pages for everyone, so this cannot be decided in Liquid —
  Liquid never sees the visitor's cookies. Instead every variant is rendered
  into the page and the browser picks one. This script runs in <head>, before
  anything paints, and stamps the answer on <html>:

    data-ll-flow      quiz | direct
    data-ll-strength  strong | medium | sensitive

  component-flow.css then shows the matching copy and hides sections that do
  not belong to the active flow. Because the choice is made by CSS on an
  attribute that is set before first paint, there is no flash of the wrong
  version.

  HOW A VISITOR BECOMES "quiz"
  ----------------------------
  The quiz writes ll_flow=quiz when it hands off to the product page
  (assets/quiz.js, assets/quiz_2.js). The strength cookie on its own is NOT
  enough: the product page's own strength picker writes one too, so a direct
  visitor who clicks around would otherwise be misread as a quiz arrival.

  Visitors who took the quiz before ll_flow existed are still recognised, by
  the starting_shade cookie — only the two quizzes ever write that.

  PREVIEWING EITHER FLOW
  ----------------------
  Add to any URL:

    ?ll_flow=quiz&ll_strength=sensitive
    ?ll_flow=direct

  The override wins over the cookies, so both flows can be checked without
  taking the quiz. In the theme editor nothing is ever hidden unless a flow is
  named in the URL this way — otherwise half the page would vanish from the
  editor and look broken.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  (function () {
    var root = document.documentElement;

    function cookie(name) {
      var m = document.cookie.match('(?:^|;\\s*)' + name + '=([^;]*)');
      return m ? decodeURIComponent(m[1]) : '';
    }

    function param(name) {
      var m = window.location.search.match('[?&]' + name + '=([^&]*)');
      return m ? decodeURIComponent(m[1]) : '';
    }

    var flowParam = param('ll_flow');
    var flow = flowParam || cookie('ll_flow');

    // Legacy quiz takers predate the ll_flow cookie; starting_shade is written
    // by the quizzes and nothing else.
    if (!flow && cookie('starting_shade')) {
      flow = 'quiz';
    }

    var strength = param('ll_strength') || cookie('strength');
    if (strength === 'gentle') {
      strength = 'sensitive';
    }
    if (strength !== 'strong' && strength !== 'medium' && strength !== 'sensitive') {
      strength = 'medium';
    }

    root.setAttribute('data-ll-flow', flow === 'quiz' ? 'quiz' : 'direct');
    root.setAttribute('data-ll-strength', strength);

    // In the editor, show every section regardless of flow unless the URL
    // explicitly asks for one, so the merchant can still see and click
    // everything they have placed.
    if (window.Shopify && window.Shopify.designMode && !flowParam) {
      root.setAttribute('data-ll-editor', 'true');
    }
  })();
</script>
